message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
title: "Animal Protection Law Database (APLD) v0.1-draft"
version: "0.1-draft"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Deng"
    given-names: "Nanyi"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-2017-049X"
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/nanyi-deng/apld"
keywords:
  - animal law
  - comparative law
  - policy surveillance
  - legal epidemiology
  - animal welfare
  - legislation
abstract: >
  A structured, provision-level dataset coding penalty structure, scope of
  application, enforcement mechanism, and linked policy-effect evidence for
  animal anti-cruelty / animal protection law across 27 jurisdictions
  (Mainland China, Taiwan, Hong Kong, Macau, Japan, South Korea, Singapore,
  United States federal, California, Texas, Canada federal, Ontario,
  Quebec, England and Wales, Scotland, Northern Ireland, the European
  Union, Germany, France, Switzerland, the Netherlands, Italy, Spain,
  Australia federal, New South Wales, Victoria, and New Zealand). Applies
  a policy-surveillance / legal-epidemiology coding methodology, not
  previously applied to this legal domain, with an explicit three-tier
  source-verification scheme (verified / snippet / unverified) shipped
  alongside the data.
